  "author_association": "OWNER",
  "body": "## Goal\n\nMake the cost view explain why API-equivalent estimates are high by showing cost contribution by token bucket.\n\n## Context\n\nCurrent live 30d provider-price estimates show the largest cost drivers are cache read and non-cache input, not output:\n\n| Component | Approx share |\n| --- | --- |\n| Cache read | ~52% |\n| Non-cache input | ~38% |\n| Output | ~10% |\n| Cache write | <1% |\n\nThis is confusing because `Total Tokens` intentionally excludes cache read/write, while cost can include priced cache tokens.\n\n## Suggested Scope\n\n- Add component cost breakdown for each model row:\n  - input cost\n  - output cost\n  - cache read cost\n  - cache write cost\n- Add a compact top-level cost-driver summary near the cost card or Model Breakdown header.\n- Make clear that `Total Tokens = non-cache input + output`, while `API-equivalent cost` can include priced cache read/write.\n- Preserve source/provider provenance: tool source is not necessarily pricing provider.\n- Keep actual billing/subscription-aware pricing tracked separately in #15.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Users can identify whether input, output, cache read, or cache write is driving the estimate.\n- Model-row cost details show component dollars when pricing is available.\n- Overview or Model Breakdown exposes aggregate cost share by component.\n- Copy avoids implying API-equivalent estimates are actual ChatGPT Pro or provider subscription charges.\n- Existing tests pass.",
